          feedback: { correct: 'Correct — the pole nearest the jω axis decays slowest and therefore persists longest.', wrong: ['Correct - the pole nearest the j-omega axis decays slowest and therefore persists longest.', 'Wrong - a pole far from the axis decays fastest and contributes only a brief initial transient.', 'Wrong - largest magnitude means fastest decay, which is the opposite of dominance.', 'Wrong - the 20:1 ratio in decay rates makes one clearly dominant.'] },
