          feedback: { correct: 'Correct — the second section draws current from the first, shifting the pole locations.', wrong: ['Correct - the second section draws current from the first, shifting the pole locations.', 'Wrong - squaring is valid only when a buffer isolates the sections.', 'Wrong - cascading multiplies transfer functions; it never adds them.', 'Wrong - the second section clearly changes the response, just not in the naive way.'] },
