          'Reciprocity and symmetry are distinct conditions that are often confused. Reciprocity means excitation and response may be interchanged, and it shows as z₁₂ = z₂₁, y₁₂ = y₂₁, h₁₂ = −h₂₁, or AD − BC = 1. Symmetry means the two ports are interchangeable — the network looks the same from either side — and it shows as z₁₁ = z₂₂, y₁₁ = y₂₂ or A = D. Every symmetric passive network is reciprocal, but the reverse does not hold: an unbalanced ladder is reciprocal and not symmetric. These conditions are worth checking on every computed parameter set, because they are free and they catch sign and arithmetic errors that would otherwise propagate.',
