        definition:
          'The input impedance of a two-port is not a property of the network alone — it depends on what terminates the far port. In terms of z parameters, Z_in = z₁₁ − z₁₂z₂₁/(z₂₂ + Z_L). The first term is the open-circuit input impedance and the second is the correction reflected back through the network by the load. The correction vanishes when Z_L is infinite, recovering z₁₁, and is largest when Z_L is zero. This is the formal version of an everyday effect: changing a loudspeaker changes what an amplifier\'s output stage sees, and changing an antenna changes what a receiver\'s input sees.',
